#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:112
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "content_profile_check: no math kind, no lean field, no .lean sibling. A paper folio has no such step; this is why a document folio needs neither Lean nor TeX to publish."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:142
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Core's shared review-and-publish process (Process_FolioReviewPublish): the reviewer reads the rendered folio and approves it, asks for changes, or sends a working draft to the Authoring Committee."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:163
#. Diagram label
msgid "Document published"
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:101
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "Every block edit runs the HCI validation gate — see editing-hci-validation.bpmn. A normative statement is a `recommendation` block, drafted through normative-statements: one statement per block, a folio-chosen label, and its strength as a code in a declared code list, so a reviewer signs off each one individually."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:93
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "folio_init writes content/, uploads/, library/, the manifests, the builder shim and AGENTS.md. Skipped when the folio already exists."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/content/authoring-a-document.bpmn:19
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "How a document folio — structured prose and policy guidance, with no Lean and no required TeX — is authored, built and reviewed end to end. Source of truth: this file. The SVG under docs/assets/img/workflows/ is generated from it by `bun run cat render:bpmn` — never hand-edit the SVG. The shape is the paper process minus the Lean lane and plus one step, the profile check, which is what keeps a document folio publishable without either toolchain. Review, publish and committee feedback are core's shared Process_FolioReviewPublish, called after rendering. Its `no` answer, changes asked, comes back to Task_AuthorBlocks."
msgstr ""

